antly told myself that i  wasn't good enough and this lasted for  about two years it was around this time  that casey neistat recognized my work  yeah and offered me a position to move  to new york and help him start a brand  called 368 which basically meant filming  his daily vlogs and attempting to edit  them constantly they're getting tired  yet dan  no  i'm good  as well as being a character of sorts in  the vlog i took on this opportunity not  only because i needed the life  experience but because i mean to have  casey neistat as a mentor is priceless  this was honest to god the hardest i've  ever worked in my entire life i would  come back to my apartment sometimes at  night and cry not knowing where this  decision was going to take me but i kept  telling myself if i just stuck to it  casey would recognize my drive and  eventually give me a platform which he  did he launched my youtube career by  making a video on his channel dedicated  to asking people to go over and  subscribe to my channel and this grew my  channel by hundreds of thousands of  people which is just nuts  i then started creating my own content  for my own youtube channel and slowly  built a community of like-minded people  from all around the world which is now  known as the brew community  i later moved back to south africa to  get married and like any business opened  up my very first office in a garage soon  after i realized with the kinds of films  i wanted to make that i could not do it  alone which leads me to the next step  when you realize that you're in a  financial position through a pipeline of  constant work you are going to need step  two people i hired my first ever  employee through sending out an  instagram post looking for an assistant  luke has now grown from being an  assistant editor to now a full-time  director for big companies like the  discovery channel luke and i then grew  to three people then four and then five  in less than a year and this was solely  from youtube 